Engineering Workflow > CI Health incidents {#broken-master} > Merging while an incident is open {#merging-during-broken-master}
If your pipeline fails only because of an open CI Health incident, wait for the fix rather than working around it. Merge trains build on top of the default branch, so an unrelated merge can add new failures and make the incident harder to track down. Don't bypass the failure unless the situation is urgent.
When the situation is urgent, there is an exception.

Authorization Matrix (2023-05) > When is Approval Required to Approve or Sign an Agreement or Contract
Any time GitLab is bound to terms and conditions, and/or, required to:
- Pay an individual (or vendor);
- Provide services / software;
- Click-through terms and conditions to gain access to a tool or resource; or
- Carry out any specific activites (e.g., keep information confidential).
Team Members must follow the applicable process to ensure all terms and obligations are reviewed and approved by specific stakeholders.
